------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6f(iii). No-information benchmark near the cutoff
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A misclassification rate is only readable against what you would get with
NO spatial information at all. The benchmark: ignore location and assign
every near-cutoff well to whichever side is more common. Its error rate is
the share on the minority side. Any method that cannot beat this is adding
nothing where the RD needs it.
   vintage n_near8 share_deep_near8 naive_error best_method best_error
    <char>   <int>            <num>       <num>      <char>      <num>
1: may1996     391            0.368      0.3683 IDW power 2     0.3785
2: may2000     419            0.368      0.3675 IDW power 2     0.3819
   improvement_pp
            <num>
1:        -0.0102
2:        -0.0143

  may1996: no-information error 36.8%; best method 37.9% -- an improvement
    of -1.0 pp.
  may2000: no-information error 36.8%; best method 38.2% -- an improvement
    of -1.4 pp.

  READING: near the cutoff, interpolation buys very little over guessing.
  The spatial signal that survives at 8 m is weak, and this is the single
  most important number in this script for the E1 decision.

